Research-Use License (mixed upstream — not for commercial use)

This model (tashkeel-nano-1p1m) is provided for RESEARCH USE ONLY.

The training data is a mix of web-scraped and paper-bundled corpora with
heterogeneous upstream licenses:

- abdou_tashkeel — compilation card claims MIT, but ~45% of its content is
  Tashkeela (commonly GPL-2 mirrored) plus shamela pages and
  GPT-4o-mini-diacritized Wikipedia.
- fadel — derives from Tashkeela.
- sadeed_tashkeela — Tashkeela-derived (GPL-2 noted), via
  HuggingFace Misraj/Sadeed_Tashkeela.
- qcri (WikiNews / Wikipedia diacritized) — paper-bundled shared data,
  citation expected.

Accordingly this model is NOT licensed for commercial use. A commercial
superset would require a real license audit of every upstream source.

You may use, study, and modify this model for research purposes. If you use
it in a project, cite the model and the upstream datasets.

Model weights: (c) 2026 the tashkeel-nano authors. Architecture: bidirectional
char-level Transformer encoder + 15-class diacritic head.
